National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Yes, we can confirm that the connection of Katanduanes is now in the TDP of NGCP. We are also looking at it, how we can prioritize that particular project since I think 2018.

2242
02:16:00,000 --> 02:16:18,520
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: So, yata ito nire-request ng FISELCO. One update also for FISELCO, Transco will now be implementing system operations in your island and hopefully we can also help in your system reliability and maybe reduce some costs also. So, that's our update for you, Mr. Gong.

2243
02:16:18,520 --> 02:16:19,670
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Great.

2244
02:16:19,670 --> 02:16:20,820
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Thank you. Thank you.

2245
02:16:21,020 --> 02:16:27,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can I interject lang? Ano yung pinakamalapit na pwede mag-submarine cable sa patang Katanduanes?

2246
02:16:28,920 --> 02:16:29,980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I'll give you the answer.

2247
02:16:30,000 --> 02:16:33,500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sir, sir. Caramoan. Distrito ko po yun.

2248
02:16:33,540 --> 02:16:35,420
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: In the TDP, I believe it's presentation.

2249
02:16:35,740 --> 02:16:48,320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah. From Karamuan, malapit na lang po kami doon. Actually, meron pong feasibility study na nakuha na kami na gagawa po ng tulay from Karamuan connecting Katanduanes.

2250
02:16:48,760 --> 02:16:58,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And kinausap ko na po yung DPWH, yung ilalim nun. Pwede po tayo maglagay doon ng linya na. So, para hindi na submarine cable, mas mahal po yun.

2251
02:16:58,260 --> 02:17:09,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, yung design na pinapagawa po namin is for the maintenance. It's a long-term plan, no? So, it's one option. I'm just telling you na yung pinakamalapit.

2252
02:17:10,040 --> 02:17:11,440
National Transmission Corporation President and CEO Atty. Joseph Omar A. Castillo: We'll take a look at that, Mr. Chair.

2253
02:17:11,440 --> 02:17:27,600
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, in addition to the schedule of the TDP, Transmission Development Plan of the NGCP, DOE also has issued a circular allowing third-party,

2254
02:17:27,600 --> 02:17:28,120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: allowing third-party,

2255
02:17:28,120 --> 02:17:43,520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: construction. But we have to work closely with NGCP on this. Transcos already identified three projects that they will embark on with the permission or the agreement to NGCP also with DOE.

2256
02:17:44,100 --> 02:17:53,660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We'll try as much as possible makuha yung approval for, para ma-advance po, na transco na yung magpapatayo. We'll work hard on that, sir.

2257
02:17:54,860 --> 02:17:57,580
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Dalawang beses na ako bumalik din dahil sa problema dyan.

2258
02:17:58,120 --> 02:18:00,600
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Maybe we can find a long-term solution, sir.

2259
02:18:00,600 --> 02:18:01,040
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Thank you.

2260
02:18:01,040 --> 02:18:09,560
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Thank you, Madam Secretary. Alam ko naman na hindi nyo paubayan ng katanduhan. Sabi nga, pabalik-balik ka na nga roon.

2261
02:18:10,040 --> 02:18:22,500
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Yun talagang problema namin. I hope itong aming tulungan ni Kung Fuente Villa na yung sa aming Princip Bridge na talagang pangarap din naman namin yun magkaroon na may tawid.

2262
02:18:23,040 --> 02:18:25,060
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: So, malay mo kung sino lang pumaw na.

2263
02:18:25,700 --> 02:18:27,520
Rep. Eulogio "Leo" R. Rodriguez: Salamat po, Mr. Chair.

2264
02:18:28,120 --> 02:18:30,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Mr. Kong Leo.

2265
02:18:30,880 --> 02:18:35,880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Basta pag nagsalita si Kong Sharon, Kong Lagrales, maniwala po tayo.

2266
02:18:37,000 --> 02:18:43,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero before I call the next interpreter, kung pwede pong magtanong rin kayo sa PNOC, pwede rin pong magsumagot.

2267
02:18:44,940 --> 02:18:49,560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, next interpreter, we have Congressman Presley Dessus.

2268
02:18:54,600 --> 02:18:57,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sinabi mo magtatanong ako, so magtatanong na ako.

2269
02:18:57,160 --> 02:18:58,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: No, in fairness, no.

2270
02:19:00,040 --> 02:19:09,040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Two points muna. Una, I'm very grateful, Congressman Dagoque, and I am grateful to Chairman Alvarez and Sen. Erwin Tupo.

2271
02:19:09,200 --> 02:19:17,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Finally, nasa Senate na at madidiscuss na September 10 yung Lineman Workers Appreciation Day.

2272
02:19:18,480 --> 02:19:21,040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, maganda yan kasi we recognize them.

2273
02:19:21,240 --> 02:19:25,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As you know, nauubos na yung mga lineman natin. Nagpupunta namin ng New Zealand at Australia.

2274
02:19:25,920 --> 02:19:29,100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, yesterday also, kinausap namin ng TESDA.

2275
02:19:29,100 --> 02:19:31,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Para tuloy-tuloy na rin yung kanilang training.

2276
02:19:32,140 --> 02:19:37,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Secondly, in fairness to Chairman ng Committee on Legislative Franchise,

2277
02:19:38,440 --> 02:19:43,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: basta't meron nagpasa ng mga ganyang prangkisa at may opposition, we give them time.

2278
02:19:44,320 --> 02:19:49,600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But he promised next time, naprubaan din yan. Just like the other electric cooperatives.

2279
02:19:50,740 --> 02:19:51,320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair? Mr. Chair?

2280
02:19:52,340 --> 02:19:53,720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Wala pa akong tanong sa 'yo?

2281
02:19:54,060 --> 02:19:56,320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I just wanted to intervene, Mr. Chair.

2282
02:19:56,360 --> 02:19:56,940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, yes.

2283
02:19:56,940 --> 02:19:58,940
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: For us, in the Department of Energy

2284
02:19:59,100 --> 02:20:05,560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And I think especially for NEA, we don't need a special day for linemen.

2285
02:20:05,800 --> 02:20:08,160
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Every day is a day for linemen, sir.

2286
02:20:08,260 --> 02:20:16,160
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Because not only do they build our infrastructure, but they are the first to go whenever there's a disaster.

2287
02:20:16,480 --> 02:20:17,500
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mga volunteers yan.

2288
02:20:17,600 --> 02:20:19,200
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: They don't have anywhere to sleep.

2289
02:20:19,300 --> 02:20:22,080
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: They just follow where the broken poles are.

2290
02:20:22,520 --> 02:20:23,500
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mga volunteer po yan.

2291
02:20:23,620 --> 02:20:24,820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pinapakain lang ng mayor.

2292
02:20:24,820 --> 02:20:28,740
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But I think they really need commendation in that sense.

2293
02:20:28,740 --> 02:20:32,460
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Because they are really the heroes of the energy family, sir.

2294
02:20:33,080 --> 02:20:33,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Well noted.

2295
02:20:34,120 --> 02:20:35,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Chairman.

2296
02:20:35,560 --> 02:20:36,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And of course, to Secretary.

2297
02:20:36,900 --> 02:20:45,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, to Secretary, when Kong Percy said a while ago, he asked you personally kung paano baaba ang kuryente.

2298
02:20:45,780 --> 02:20:47,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And you said, there's a formula.

2299
02:20:48,640 --> 02:20:52,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Siguro, nung 18 Congress kami, yan na inaan namin talaga hindi bumaba ba.

2300
02:20:52,600 --> 02:20:54,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Aside from the inflation rate.

2301
02:20:54,020 --> 02:20:57,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, siguro this time, yun nga, yung system loss natin.

2302
02:20:58,740 --> 02:21:04,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tanong ko, is it time ng generation, the gencos, should be regulated na?

2303
02:21:06,810 --> 02:21:09,210
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Although we know in EPIRA, hindi.

2304
02:21:09,630 --> 02:21:11,350
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Pero, it's high time, is it?

2305
02:21:12,090 --> 02:21:16,850
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, I do not think that we need to regulate.

2306
02:21:17,850 --> 02:21:21,390
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But we need to have safeguards, Mr. Chair.

2307
02:21:21,390 --> 02:21:29,230
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: For example, once you have a COC, you have the permit, you have the permit forever.

2308
02:21:29,230 --> 02:21:31,050
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Regardless of your performance.

2309
02:21:31,410 --> 02:21:40,930
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And that's why we are issuing new policies now to have more accountability for the gencos.

2310
02:21:41,070 --> 02:21:46,410
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Kasi minsan, nakalista yan sa profile natin, sa energy mix natin.

2311
02:21:46,830 --> 02:21:49,910
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pero, mga four months a year lang pala siya nandun.

2312
02:21:50,310 --> 02:21:51,630
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And there has to be accountability.

2313
02:21:52,030 --> 02:21:53,990
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Dapat siya nagahanap ng replacement power.

2314
02:21:53,990 --> 02:21:57,910
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, there are things that have been missing over the years.

2315
02:21:58,610 --> 02:21:58,990
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And we...

2316
02:21:59,230 --> 02:22:06,010
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We need to be more strict in a sense that they have to comply with whatever is required by EPIRA,

2317
02:22:06,090 --> 02:22:10,110
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: whatever is required by ERC, and the PSA or the contract they entered.

2318
02:22:10,250 --> 02:22:13,350
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, papunta na kami dyan, Mr. Chair.

2319
02:22:13,350 --> 02:22:26,090
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And I think if we do regulate, we might dislodge the investment appetite in that sense.

2320
02:22:26,710 --> 02:22:29,130
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pero, kailangan talaga medyo may mga regulator.

2321
02:22:29,230 --> 02:22:30,170
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Sorry, powers tayo.

2322
02:22:30,910 --> 02:22:32,670
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2323
02:22:32,750 --> 02:22:38,390
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Of course, when Congressman Jokno asked about this solar para sa bayan,

2324
02:22:39,570 --> 02:22:42,570
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: noong 18th Congress, di pa kami congressman ni Kogdagi.

2325
02:22:42,730 --> 02:22:44,990
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kami ang nagra-rally na huwag pagbigyan yan.

2326
02:22:45,690 --> 02:22:46,790
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi alam namin mangyayari.

2327
02:22:46,910 --> 02:22:49,350
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Look what happened to Occidental Mindoro.

2328
02:22:49,650 --> 02:22:51,210
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kawain lang nilagay nilang poste.

2329
02:22:51,550 --> 02:22:56,430
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, when you said, you know, balitan-balitan, 24 billion nilang ano.

2330
02:22:58,070 --> 02:22:59,210
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I think hindi yun ang problem.

2331
02:22:59,230 --> 02:23:05,670
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ang problema dun, did they deliver what is stated in their service contract na magdi-deliver siya ng supply?

2332
02:23:08,260 --> 02:23:13,560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: You're correct, Mr. Chair, in a sense that because of, how many megawatts yun?

2333
02:23:15,700 --> 02:23:18,040
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: These are about 33 contracts.

2334
02:23:18,940 --> 02:23:20,580
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Most of it under GAYA.

2335
02:23:21,300 --> 02:23:26,380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And had those, it's about 1.3 gigawatts.

2336
02:23:26,460 --> 02:23:29,340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Had those 1.3 gigawatts been delivered,

2337
02:23:29,340 --> 02:23:35,740
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: according to our simulation, there would have been a decrease in the price, about 2 pesos ba?

2338
02:23:36,520 --> 02:23:37,460
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: 1 peso.

2339
02:23:37,700 --> 02:23:41,820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: 1 peso at the very least on the generation rate natin, sir.

2340
02:23:42,220 --> 02:23:49,120
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, that's, it's not the penalty itself, but it's the cost to our consumers na nangyari.

2341
02:23:49,280 --> 02:23:52,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: See, that's the problem, Chairman, because you gave the service contract.

2342
02:23:52,560 --> 02:23:56,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, walang pwedeng umago dun until such time na mag-deliver sila ng ano.

2343
02:23:56,540 --> 02:23:59,100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, do you see?

2344
02:23:59,100 --> 02:24:04,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In the foreseeable future, magkakaroon kayo ng cancellation of service contracts na hindi pa na-umpisan?

2345
02:24:05,400 --> 02:24:11,480
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Mr. Chair, all the contracts we are being reviewed, we're cleaning it up.

2346
02:24:11,480 --> 02:24:16,680
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We have cancelled so far about 100 plus, 200 contracts already.

2347
02:24:17,240 --> 02:24:19,820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: That's for the service contracts on renewable energy.

2348
02:24:20,020 --> 02:24:27,320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yung hindi gumagalaw, yung wall, late na siya, or wala siyang, ano tawag dito?

2349
02:24:28,020 --> 02:24:29,080
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Hindi siya may-aral.

2350
02:24:29,100 --> 02:24:29,680
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Hindi siya may-aral ng lote.

2351
02:24:29,800 --> 02:24:31,380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Wala siyang tenorial, ano?

2352
02:24:31,680 --> 02:24:32,520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Posesory, right.

2353
02:24:33,180 --> 02:24:35,520
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we're cancelling, starting to cancel that.

2354
02:24:35,960 --> 02:24:43,700
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And then, on the, and then next is we issue the GENCO accountability na kailangan may warning naman.

2355
02:24:43,940 --> 02:24:48,160
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pag hindi ka mag-comply ng requirements ng DOE or ERC, strike 1 ka.

2356
02:24:48,540 --> 02:24:56,560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Next strike, up to strike 3 ka, we can cancel the COE or blacklist you.

2357
02:24:56,560 --> 02:24:58,560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, we are trying to have more discipline.

2358
02:24:59,100 --> 02:25:02,200
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: In the generation companies, Mr. Chair.

2359
02:25:03,000 --> 02:25:04,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2360
02:25:04,480 --> 02:25:05,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, maybe in the second round.

2361
02:25:06,420 --> 02:25:08,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sa ERC, kay Commissioner, no?

2362
02:25:09,160 --> 02:25:14,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As you know, balitang-balita sa besides, you mentioned it's also a while ago na yellow-red alert na naman tayo.

2363
02:25:15,580 --> 02:25:18,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, what happened sa mga plantang sarado doon?

2364
02:25:19,320 --> 02:25:20,440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And how many of them?

2365
02:25:27,120 --> 02:25:27,480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yan siya.

2366
02:25:32,560 --> 02:25:33,040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

2367
02:25:33,680 --> 02:25:35,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: If our director for...

2368
02:25:36,400 --> 02:25:37,120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ano?

2369
02:25:38,520 --> 02:25:39,200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ERC?

2370
02:25:39,400 --> 02:25:49,080
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Ang mga naka-outage po sa Visayas lalo na would include the Therma Visayas at yung PEDC.

2371
02:25:49,600 --> 02:26:01,560
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: But, nag-announce naman ang TVI na it will be resuming operations September 15 at yung Unit 2 na-restore noong August 31.

2372
02:26:02,560 --> 02:26:10,130
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, bukod dito, may mga naka-outage pa ring mga ibang maliliit na planta and tuloy-tuloy.

2373
02:26:10,130 --> 02:26:13,450
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And we will check on the status po of these plants.

2374
02:26:14,730 --> 02:26:19,470
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Alam mo kung ilang planta and how many megawatts na hindi sila nakapag-deliver?

2375
02:26:22,060 --> 02:26:23,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: A big thing.

2376
02:26:27,320 --> 02:26:28,040
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Let me see.

2377
02:26:28,600 --> 02:26:31,840
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Yung each unit of TVI is 176.

2378
02:26:31,940 --> 02:26:32,720
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, dalawa sila.

2379
02:26:32,720 --> 02:26:41,200
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Kaya, nung ngayong naka-outage sila, medyo malaki talaga yung nawawala sa available supplies sa Visayas lalo na.

2380
02:26:41,560 --> 02:26:43,720
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: That's why we are seeing the yellow...

2381
02:26:44,000 --> 02:26:46,020
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: red alerts in the region.

2382
02:26:48,100 --> 02:26:51,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Alam mo, dito tayo naintindihan natin line rental eh.

2383
02:26:51,400 --> 02:26:52,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can you explain yung layman's term?

2384
02:26:53,780 --> 02:26:56,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: You suspended August 16 yung line rental, di ba?

2385
02:26:59,260 --> 02:27:00,700
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Yes po, Mr. Chair.

2386
02:27:00,780 --> 02:27:07,300
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: During periods where the interconnection is congested, Visayas and Mindanao,

2387
02:27:09,860 --> 02:27:13,360
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: dahil doon natin nakikita nagkakaroon ng spike sa line rental,

2388
02:27:14,000 --> 02:27:18,600
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: we asked IMOP to suspend the calculation and collection of the line rental

2389
02:27:18,600 --> 02:27:23,180
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and then just collect the necessary amounts from the customers

2390
02:27:23,180 --> 02:27:25,480
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: para mabayaran yung mga generators.

2391
02:27:25,480 --> 02:27:32,940
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: But as a long-term solution, there is something to be done doon sa data

2392
02:27:32,940 --> 02:27:43,480
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: that will be inputted in the CRSS so that the correct allocation of NSS surplus

2393
02:27:44,000 --> 02:27:47,140
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: to the customers will be done.

2394
02:27:47,880 --> 02:27:55,540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And we also ask IMOP to recalculate, to cost the audit through a third party

2395
02:27:55,540 --> 02:28:04,040
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: of the payments or the NSS allocations made over the period from 2021

2396
02:28:04,040 --> 02:28:11,540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: so that we can determine if there will be a need to order some refunds

2397
02:28:12,140 --> 02:28:13,540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: in favor of...

2398
02:28:14,000 --> 02:28:18,720
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: some distribution utilities who should have received a higher percentage

2399
02:28:18,720 --> 02:28:22,020
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: or higher allocation of the NSS.

2400
02:28:22,920 --> 02:28:23,500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you.

2401
02:28:23,600 --> 02:28:24,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I'll just come back with you.

2402
02:28:25,400 --> 02:28:29,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, to Secretary, you know the ER-194 natin, di ba?

2403
02:28:30,320 --> 02:28:32,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: You know how much you have right now?

2404
02:28:32,480 --> 02:28:32,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kung kano?

2405
02:28:34,680 --> 02:28:36,940
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: It's one centavo per...

2406
02:28:36,940 --> 02:28:37,200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I know.

2407
02:28:37,260 --> 02:28:37,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How much in total?

